title: Find the moment first, from file times; then read the requests around it.
pid: dc0c50f9-91f7-4576-a566-fa0a1a7c2cac
body: |2-
  A '.skg' file's mtime is when a save (or an editor, or git) wrote it, and a note
  Jeff writes about a bug has one too.
  'find DATAROOT -name "*.skg" -newermt "2026-11-13 20:34" -printf "%TT %p\n" | sort'
  lists what changed after a time. The run folder whose START comes before the
  moment holds its log. A file's owner group and mode say only whether it was
  created or overwritten, not who wrote it. The diff view's before-graph is each
  owned skgrepo's HEAD, not the git index, so a staged change is still a change.
